      "extract": "The domain wall ring can be linearly extended to a domain wall tube in d = 3 + 1 dimensions. Here we further consider a closed domain wall tube, i.e., a toroidal domain wall. Such a toroidal domain wall is unstable unless the U(1) modulus is twisted along the torus. Therefore, we twist the U(1) modulus along the torus, resulting in a doubly twisted toroidal domain wall. First, let us put a charge Q (or −Q) lump in",
